sam: Heads up — Next.js Edge middleware failing when using the SDK in a middleware because of missing Node crypto/subtle.

maria: Repro? stack trace?

sam: error: "crypto.subtle is not a function" from SDK's auth signing at runtime. Happens only in edge middleware (vercel). local node dev + server works.

kevin: Is SDK pulling in Node 'crypto' via require() anywhere? Edge runtime expects Web Crypto on globalThis.

sam: Yes, sdk's signing uses `import { randomBytes } from 'crypto'` in one helper we ship.

jules: We should ship an edge-friendly build. Quick workaround: polyfill with webcrypto wrapper in middleware before importing SDK: :wrench:

```js
// middleware.js (Next Edge)
if (!globalThis.crypto) {
  // NOTE: dynamic import of node 'crypto' will fail on Vercel Edge — only works in Node servers
  import('crypto').then(c => { globalThis.crypto = c.webcrypto });
}
// lazy import SDK after shim
const { RedwoodSDK } = await import('redwood-inference/sdk-edge.mjs');
```

maria: That import('crypto') will fail on Vercel Edge though (no node imports). I think better: use a small runtime shim that only references WebCrypto methods already available in the Edge runtime.

```js
// edge-crypto-shim.mjs
export function ensureWebCrypto() {
  if (!globalThis.crypto || !globalThis.crypto.subtle) {
    // if missing, throw so devs know to pick an environment with Web Crypto
    throw new Error('Edge runtime missing Web Crypto APIs');
  }
  return globalThis.crypto;
}
```

kevin: For TypeScript, also need `lib` DOM in tsconfig or types won't match. Add: `"lib": ["ES2021","DOM"]` and set `module: "esnext"`.

sam: Can we change SDK package.json to add an export path for edge to a tiny ESM build that uses WebCrypto APIs and avoids Node imports? That would eliminate user shims.

jules: Agreed — plan: add `"./edge": "./dist/edge/index.mjs"` in `exports` + produce `dist/edge` build that replaces Node crypto with WebCrypto wrappers, and ship `dist/edge/index.d.ts`. Also add CI check that runs minimal Next Edge handler smoke test.

sdk-bot: Created issue #1324: "edge: provide WebCrypto-only build + docs for Next.js middleware" — assigned to kevin, jules. :white_check_mark:

sam: Thanks — for now I'll add the shim snippet to our dev docs and the onboarding sample app so customers hitting Edge get an explicit pointer.

maria: Also add a short note in the SDK README about Next.js Edge constraints (no fs, no node built-ins) + recommended tsconfig. That should cut onboarding friction. :+1:
